course: dictionary
lesson: 12030
title: Chopped
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chop means to cut something into pieces with a knife or an axe. «Mum chopped the carrots for the soup.» Chopped is the past form of chop, so it tells you the cutting happened earlier, not now.
explain: Chopped can describe food too. «Finely chopped» means cut into very small pieces. «Sam added finely chopped parsley to the sauce.» Finely tells you the pieces are tiny.
explain: Use the words around chopped to check its meaning. «The woodcutter chopped the old log.» Woodcutters use an axe, so chopped means cut with an axe, and the log was split into pieces.
fact: Chop means to cut something into pieces, usually with a knife or an axe.
fact: Chopped is the past form of chop: yesterday Sam chopped the carrots, and today he chops them.
fact: «Finely chopped» means cut into very small pieces.
fact: «Chopped» can also mean cut off or removed suddenly, as in «the scene was chopped from the film».
fact: Always chop with an adult and keep your fingers away from the blade.
exercise: «Dad chopped the onions into small pieces.» What does chopped mean? | Cooked slowly in a pot | *Cut into pieces | Bought from a shop | Washed clean
exercise: «The cook added finely chopped herbs to the soup.» What does finely chopped mean? | Frozen solid | Left whole and uncut | Put in a bag | *Cut into very small pieces
exercise: Which tool could be used to chop wood? | Spoon | *Axe | Pencil | Pillow
test: «The woodcutter chopped wood all morning.» What did the woodcutter do to the wood? | Dropped it in the river | Counted it | Painted it | *Cut it into pieces
test: Which word is the past form of chop? | chopping | chop | *chopped | chops
exam: «Ella chopped the apples carefully and kept her fingers away from the blade.» Why did Ella keep her fingers away from the blade? | To stop the apples from rolling | *To keep her fingers safe from the sharp blade | To make the apples bigger | To hold the apples still for a photo
